## 3. Explicit 29-gate Stinespring word

Use little-endian logical wire order `P=0,M=1,B=2,R=3,A=4`, and write

```text
Ry(theta) = [[cos(theta/2),-sin(theta/2)],
             [sin(theta/2), cos(theta/2)]].
```

The circuit uses controlled `Ry`, CNOT, and the existing exact 15-gate
H/T/CNOT Toffoli decomposition. A doubly controlled rotation is decomposed as

```text
CRy_(c2,t)(a/2)
CNOT_(c1,c2)
CRy_(c2,t)(-a/2)
CNOT_(c1,c2)
CRy_(c1,t)(a/2).
```

The complete word is:

1. `CRy_(P,B)(pi/2)`;
2. `CCRy_(P,M;B)(2 atan2(2,1)-pi/2)`;
3. `CNOT_(B,M)`, temporarily forming `q=M xor B`;
4. `CCRy_(P,q;R)(2 atan2(sqrt(2),sqrt(5)))`;
5. `CNOT_(R,A)`, purifying the rank-two middle output;
6. `CNOT_(B,M)`, restoring `M`; and
7. `Toffoli_(M,B;R)`, setting the `h=2` prepared output.

Counting each doubly controlled rotation as five and the Toffoli as fifteen
gives exactly 29 one-/two-M2 gates. Its clean-subspace isometry is

```text
|0,0,000> -> |0,0,0,0,0>
|0,1,000> -> |0,1,0,0,0>

|1,0,000> ->
    1/sqrt(2) |1,0,0,0,0>
  + sqrt(5/14)|1,0,1,0,0>
  + sqrt(1/7) |1,0,1,1,1>

|1,1,000> ->
    sqrt(1/7)  |1,1,0,0,0>
  + sqrt(2/35) |1,1,0,1,1>
  + 2/sqrt(5)  |1,1,1,1,0>.
```

The runner constructs the full `32 x 32` unitary from the gate matrices and
compares its four clean columns to these analytic columns. Unitarity and
isometry residuals are numerical only because the displayed square-root
rotations are evaluated in double precision; both are required below
`5e-11`.

